      "description": "Watch Deportivo Alavés vs Villarreal highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The floodlights shone brightly on August 28, 2026, as Deportivo Alavés welcomed Villarreal for a high-stakes La Liga encounter. Both sides sought to establish their rhythm early in a match defined by contrasting tactical approaches in front of a crowd of 15,556. The Clinical Breakthrough Despite Villarreal maintaining an overwhelming 76% of possession for much of the game, it was Deportivo Alavés who demonstrated the true meaning of efficiency. In the 31st minute, a masterfully executed team move carved open the Yellow Submarine's defense. Antonio Blanco provided the line-breaking pass to Angel Pérez , who squared it for Lucas Boyé . The striker made no mistake, finishing clinically with his right foot to send the home fans into raptures. Villarreal attempted to muster an immediate response, but they found the Alavés defensive block impossible to penetrate. Juan Foyth saw a header blocked just before the interval, a moment that epitomized the frustration of the visitors as their intricate passing patterns failed to yield results in the final third. Drama and the Denied Woodwork The second half evolved into a tense tactical battle of attrition. Deportivo Alavés nearly doubled their lead in the 70th minute when Angel Pérez found space in the box, only to see his powerful effort crash against the post. This close shave sparked a flurry of tactical changes from the visitors, with Ayoze Pérez and Ilias Akhomach introduced to provide a much-needed spark. However, the woodwork would prove to be the enemy of both sides. In the 85th minute, Juan Foyth came agonizingly close to an equalizer, but his finish also struck the post. As the clock ticked down, the atmosphere grew increasingly heated. The referee was forced to reach for his pocket frequently, cautioning Nicolas Pépé , Mariano Díaz , and Renato Veiga as challenges became more desperate. Standing Firm Under Pressure In a frantic period of stoppage time, Villarreal threw everything forward. Jonny Otto fired wide from distance, and Juan Foyth missed the target with another header in the dying seconds. Deportivo Alavés goalkeeper Antonio Sivera received a yellow card for time-wasting, a testament to the pressure his side was under. When the final whistle eventually blew, it confirmed a hard-fought victory built on defensive discipline and clinical finishing, leaving the possession-heavy visitors empty-handed."
